# Keep the Docker build context to source only.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY src ./src` and `COPY frontend ./frontend`, so
# anything lying around in the working tree ends up inside the build. Host
# build output is the dangerous case: `obj/project.assets.json` records
# absolute NuGet paths from the machine that produced it, so a tree built on
# Windows (or simply on the host rather than in the container) will point the
# in-container restore at paths that do not exist and fail the build.
#
# Everything listed here is regenerated inside the image, so excluding it is
# also a straight speed win -- a polluted context can be hundreds of MB.

# --- build output (regenerated in-container) ---
_output/
_temp/
_tests/
_appdata/
**/bin/
**/obj/

# --- dependencies (restored in-container) ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# --- version control & CI ---
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github/
.devcontainer/

# --- editor / OS ---
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- docs & packaging not needed to build the app ---
distribution/
*.md
!README.md

# --- local runtime config, never baked into an image ---
config/
test-library/
docker-compose*.yml
